WEBVTT

00:05.011 --> 00:07.878
I said no.
And I say, why not?

00:08.047 --> 00:10.277
- Why not?
I don't have to give you a reason.

00:10.483 --> 00:13.350
Dad, I got my learner's permit
but Mom won't let me drive.

00:13.520 --> 00:17.012
Just because they give 15-year-olds permits
doesn't mean they're ready.

00:17.190 --> 00:18.851
I've been driving for years.

00:19.025 --> 00:21.550
"Grand Theft Auto 1,"
"Grand Theft Auto 2."

00:22.862 --> 00:25.456
I never ran over anybody
but pimps and crack whores.

00:25.632 --> 00:28.692
- Jake.
- Sorry, crack prostitutes.

00:29.702 --> 00:31.192
Go get started on your homework.

00:31.371 --> 00:33.601
- After, will you take me driving?
- We'll talk.

00:33.773 --> 00:34.967
- When?
- Go to your room.

00:35.141 --> 00:37.541
- I'm available now.
- Go.

00:37.710 --> 00:41.737
Man, if I knew how to hot-wire a real car,
I'd be so out of here.

00:42.749 --> 00:46.446
- Thanks for bringing him by, I guess.
- Lf you need to reach me, Herb and I...

00:46.619 --> 00:49.053
...are going to Laguna Beach
for a weekend getaway.

00:49.255 --> 00:52.247
- How nice. Taking the baby?
- Are you insane? I said "getaway."

00:52.425 --> 00:53.824
Herb's lucky I'm taking him.

00:54.561 --> 00:58.088
- I see. So who's watching little Millie?
- My mother.

00:58.264 --> 01:02.724
- Ooh. Are we sure that's a good idea?
- Okay, first of all, there is no we here.

01:02.902 --> 01:04.096
And what are you implying?

01:04.270 --> 01:07.501
That there might be better choices
for a babysitter than a woman...

01:07.674 --> 01:10.905
...who has a sandwich named after her
at the Betty Ford clinic.

01:12.779 --> 01:15.942
She's three years clean and sober,
all the charges were dropped...

01:16.115 --> 01:18.583
...and she's great with Millie.
- All right.

01:18.751 --> 01:21.413
I gave her your number,
in case there's an emergency.

01:21.588 --> 01:24.318
I don't mind. So how is the baby anyway?

01:25.291 --> 01:26.758
- Fine.
- Good, good.

01:26.926 --> 01:28.757
Jake showed me some pictures.

01:28.928 --> 01:31.158
I gotta say,
she doesn't look much like you...

01:31.331 --> 01:33.196
...and she doesn't look like Herb.

01:33.366 --> 01:34.993
Don't go there, Alan.

01:35.168 --> 01:38.001
Go where? I'm not implying that
someone other than Herb...

01:38.171 --> 01:40.639
...could be the father,
even though that someone...

01:40.807 --> 01:44.641
...did have unprotected sex with you
nine months before the birth of a child...

01:44.811 --> 01:47.371
...that looks suspiciously
like that someone.

01:48.314 --> 01:50.373
You get that I'm talking about me, right?

01:50.550 --> 01:52.984
If we wanna beat the traffic,
we should get going.

01:53.152 --> 01:54.176
- Hey, Alan.
- Hey, Herb.

01:54.354 --> 01:57.790
You hear? Judith and I are spending
a romantic weekend in Laguna.

01:57.957 --> 02:00.016
I said weekend, Herb. That's all.

02:00.193 --> 02:03.026
Okay, fine, no romance.

02:03.196 --> 02:05.187
But sex is still on the table, right?

02:05.365 --> 02:07.356
- Just get in the car.
- Oh, can I drive?

02:07.533 --> 02:09.467
- No.
- Why not?

02:11.371 --> 02:12.998
Is she gone?

02:15.642 --> 02:17.109
Damn it!

02:19.412 --> 02:21.471
Chelsea, your cat's trying to kill me.

02:21.648 --> 02:24.014
Is he okay?
- The cat's fine.

02:24.183 --> 02:28.017
Probably off plotting his next mo...
Whoa. Whoa!

02:28.187 --> 02:30.212
- Are you okay?
- No.

02:30.990 --> 02:32.651
- What happened?
- Uncle Charlie fell.

02:32.825 --> 02:34.053
Oh.

02:34.227 --> 02:36.252
Can I drive you to the hospital?

03:06.125 --> 03:08.093
Mr. Lancelot!

03:09.996 --> 03:12.157
Here, kitty, kitty!

03:14.400 --> 03:17.062
He's probably hiding
because he thinks you're mad at him.

03:18.438 --> 03:21.999
For God's sake, the cat doesn't think
anything except maybe:

03:22.175 --> 03:23.938
"Mm, fish, I'll eat it."

03:25.411 --> 03:28.437
Or, "Ooh, sand, I'll crap in it."

03:29.115 --> 03:32.141
You're wrong.
He's very intelligent and very intuitive.

03:32.318 --> 03:36.345
- He knows you resent him living here.
- Thank you, but I can defend myself.

03:38.758 --> 03:40.123
I was talking about my cat.

03:40.293 --> 03:43.626
Oh. Oh, I'm sorry. Mm, fish, yum.

03:45.798 --> 03:50.292
- Okay, I'm going to work. Feel better.
- Thanks.

03:50.470 --> 03:51.698
How's the shoulder?

03:53.439 --> 03:54.929
Oh, the shoulder's fine.

03:55.108 --> 03:58.043
I'm just hoping to get a little
"Oh, poor Charlie" tonight.

03:58.211 --> 04:03.615
- "Oh, poor Charlie?"
- Yeah. You know, "Oh, poor Charlie.

04:03.783 --> 04:07.048
I feel bad about your shoulder,
so you just lie still...

04:07.220 --> 04:10.212
...while I provide you
with a series of intense orgasms."

04:11.791 --> 04:15.386
Wow. I don't know what to say,
other than "oink."

04:17.296 --> 04:18.854
Is that a car? Can I drive?

04:19.031 --> 04:20.760
Relax, it was just Chelsea going to work.

04:20.933 --> 04:23.197
Oh. Uncle Charlie,
you need to go anywhere?

04:23.369 --> 04:26.827
- Yeah, away from you.
- All right. I'll drive you.

04:28.007 --> 04:30.703
You wanna drive my $80,000 Mercedes?

04:30.877 --> 04:32.572
Yes, please.

04:32.745 --> 04:36.545
It's good that he's polite.
It's a necessary quality in a doorman.

04:38.050 --> 04:40.848
- Was that a yes or a no?
- That was a no.

04:41.020 --> 04:44.046
- So the doorman thing was an insult?
- Yes.

04:44.457 --> 04:45.549
Oh.

04:48.060 --> 04:49.220
And a prophecy.

04:54.200 --> 04:55.758
Hello?

04:55.968 --> 04:58.266
No, it's Charlie. Who's this?

04:58.905 --> 05:00.930
I can't hear you, what?

05:02.308 --> 05:03.332
- Alan, it's for you.
- Oh.

05:05.278 --> 05:09.908
Hello? Oh. Oh, hi, Lenore.
It's Judith's mother.

05:10.082 --> 05:12.778
Is that the house alarm?

05:12.985 --> 05:15.385
Is the baby okay?

05:16.556 --> 05:19.389
All right, open the little panel
by the front door...

05:19.559 --> 05:22.892
...and enter pound, star and the code.

05:24.564 --> 05:26.794
Pound is the little tic-tac-toe board.

05:28.468 --> 05:31.767
&lt;i>Yeah, like on Hollywood Squares.&lt;/i>

05:32.572 --> 05:34.938
- She still popping the pain pills?
- No.

05:35.107 --> 05:37.302
Good. See if she's got any leftovers.

05:38.644 --> 05:41.636
Okay, the code is Jake's birthday.

05:42.882 --> 05:45.112
Your grandson.

05:45.751 --> 05:49.915
Anyway, it's 0314. Oh.
No, Lenore, don't punch it into the phone.

05:50.089 --> 05:52.751
No, Lenore! Lenore! Lenore.
Okay, okay, okay. Calm down.

05:52.925 --> 05:56.383
Calm down. I'll be right there.
I will turn it off for you.

05:56.562 --> 05:59.793
Okay, okay. Bye. Ugh. I gotta go.

05:59.966 --> 06:03.629
You couldn't be more of a sucker
if you were on the end of a stick.

06:03.803 --> 06:07.136
Why? Because I'll take any excuse
to spend time with my daughter?

06:07.306 --> 06:10.400
- You don't know you're the father.
- Oh, come on.

06:10.576 --> 06:13.067
She's got my jaw line, my eyes, my ears.

06:13.246 --> 06:16.010
You left out thinning hair
and poopy pants.

06:17.450 --> 06:20.578
That was one time
and I begged you to stop at a gas station.

06:27.360 --> 06:29.828
Oh, Alan, thank God you're here.

06:29.996 --> 06:33.090
I pushed all the buttons,
but I can't get it to stop.

06:33.266 --> 06:37.362
That might be because you were
adjusting the thermostat.

06:41.507 --> 06:44.670
- Ah. There we go.
- Oh, thank God.

06:44.844 --> 06:48.644
Oh, here, let me see if I can turn
this alarm off, ha, ha. Come here, Millie.

06:48.814 --> 06:49.940
Come to Papa.

06:53.452 --> 06:56.819
&lt;i>Was a rolling stone&lt;/i>

06:56.989 --> 07:01.187
&lt;i>Wherever he laid his hat was his home&lt;/i>

07:01.360 --> 07:05.023
Always sang this to Jake.
Worked like a charm.

07:05.731 --> 07:08.632
&lt;i>And when he died&lt;/i>

07:08.801 --> 07:11.827
&lt;i>All he left us was alone&lt;/i>

07:13.339 --> 07:17.241
- Huh. Look at that.
- Well, you are a miracle worker, Alan.

07:17.410 --> 07:21.403
Oh, no. I just have a knack for babies.
And animals.

07:21.614 --> 07:24.515
It's only English-speaking adults
that don't like me.

07:25.117 --> 07:27.415
Well, I think you're a wonderful fellow.

07:27.620 --> 07:31.181
And if you don't mind my saying,
Judith was a fool to let you go.

07:31.357 --> 07:34.485
Eh. She didn't so much let me go
as drop me from an airplane...

07:34.660 --> 07:36.855
...with an anvil necklace.

07:37.997 --> 07:40.693
Okay, honey,
time to get your beauty rest.

07:40.866 --> 07:44.996
I'm afraid that's gonna have
to be a long nap.

07:45.171 --> 07:47.196
I hate to say it about my granddaughter...

07:47.373 --> 07:52.572
...but let's face it, with those big ears,
she looks a little like a fruit bat.

07:54.747 --> 07:56.681
I think her ears are the perfect size.

07:57.550 --> 07:58.608
You would.

07:59.885 --> 08:04.379
- How about some wine?
- Uh... Thank you, but I should get going.

08:04.557 --> 08:07.856
Oh, no, come on. Join me.
Just one. We'll catch up.

08:08.027 --> 08:12.088
Uh, it's none of my business,
but do you think you should be drinking?

08:13.099 --> 08:15.966
- Because I've been to Betty Ford?
- Oh, no.

08:16.168 --> 08:18.966
Because you got kicked out of Betty Ford.

08:19.138 --> 08:20.901
Hey, Britney bit me first.

08:22.908 --> 08:26.105
Anyway, I was there for pills.

08:26.278 --> 08:29.270
I've never had a problem with alcohol.

08:34.086 --> 08:36.554
See? No problem.

08:36.989 --> 08:39.287
Okay, now...

08:39.458 --> 08:44.225
...where did I hide those muscle relaxers
I picked up in Mexico?

08:47.700 --> 08:51.158
That's right, between my butt cheeks.

08:54.140 --> 08:55.607
Turn around.

09:10.056 --> 09:11.080
Uncle Charlie?

09:11.257 --> 09:13.657
- What?
- You hungry?

09:15.528 --> 09:18.691
Because if you are,
we could go get something to eat.

09:18.864 --> 09:20.525
And I'll even drive.

09:21.434 --> 09:24.631
- Jake, I'm sleeping.
- Okay.

09:28.307 --> 09:30.207
You know, you can nap in the car.

09:30.376 --> 09:33.709
I just gotta have an adult with me.
They don't have to be conscious.

09:34.447 --> 09:37.939
- I'm not hungry.
- Okay, fine.

09:41.320 --> 09:43.948
You wanna go see a movie?
Because if you do...

09:46.192 --> 09:47.955
Maybe after your nap.

09:52.765 --> 09:58.635
- Oh, crap, now I'm awake.
- Great. You hungry?

10:01.340 --> 10:04.138
You're lucky you're single, Alan.

10:04.310 --> 10:06.870
- Oh, I don't know.
- Oh, no, trust me.

10:07.046 --> 10:10.243
I've been married for 39 years.

10:12.718 --> 10:14.879
Really? But Judith's 40.

10:15.054 --> 10:16.885
Shh.

10:18.924 --> 10:23.725
Do you know what it's like to wake up
every morning, year after year...

10:23.896 --> 10:28.390
...and see the same stupid face
lying next to you?

10:29.568 --> 10:32.935
Uh, well, all I can tell you
is what I told your daughter.

10:33.105 --> 10:35.903
If you don't like it, roll over.

10:39.912 --> 10:42.745
Fred hasn't touched me in 14 years.

10:42.915 --> 10:47.443
Uh, well, in his defense,
he did have that stroke.

10:48.287 --> 10:51.347
Do you know what happens
to a woman's body...

10:51.524 --> 10:53.583
...when it goes unloved for that long?

10:53.759 --> 10:56.922
Lenore, I don't feel comfortable
talking about this with you.

10:57.096 --> 10:59.394
Oh, now, Alan, come on.
We're both grown-ups.

10:59.565 --> 11:02.534
Think about what I am saying.

11:05.738 --> 11:07.603
All right? Well...

11:09.375 --> 11:14.779
&lt;i>I'm getting an image of a cave
from an Indiana Jones movie.&lt;/i>

11:15.548 --> 11:16.572
What?

11:17.550 --> 11:21.111
Well, you know, cobwebs...

11:21.554 --> 11:23.647
...dust...

11:23.856 --> 11:25.721
...human skulls.

11:26.358 --> 11:29.794
This is my vagina we're talking about.

11:29.962 --> 11:33.227
Oh, I am well aware
of what we're talking about.

11:34.967 --> 11:37.595
I've been so alone.

11:38.103 --> 11:40.901
Oh. Oh. I'm...

11:41.173 --> 11:42.936
I'm sorry, Lenore.

11:57.990 --> 11:59.821
A stroke's starting to look pretty good.

12:06.298 --> 12:08.926
- Can't I at least back it out?
- No.

12:09.101 --> 12:10.966
Come on, nothing's gonna happen.

12:12.338 --> 12:14.238
- Look, you wanna go eat or not?
- Fine.

12:14.406 --> 12:16.772
If we went to an empty parking lot,
could I drive?

12:16.942 --> 12:18.273
How many times I gotta tell you...?

12:23.582 --> 12:26.813
- What the hell was that?
- I don't know.

12:26.986 --> 12:28.510
Sounds like you ran over a cat.

12:38.063 --> 12:39.928
Told you you should have let me drive.

12:42.301 --> 12:44.735
You know,
Chelsea's gonna completely freak out.

12:44.904 --> 12:47.964
No, she will not be happy.

12:49.408 --> 12:52.639
- Doesn't even look like a cat anymore.
- Nope.

12:52.811 --> 12:56.474
More like a cat pancake. "Catcake."

12:57.983 --> 12:59.644
Sorry.

12:59.818 --> 13:03.219
- What am I gonna tell her?
- She doesn't have to know.

13:03.856 --> 13:05.050
You're right.

13:05.224 --> 13:07.920
She thinks Sir Lancelot's missing,
so he stays missing.

13:08.093 --> 13:10.721
Sir Squished-a-Lot.

13:10.896 --> 13:12.557
Let's think what we've gotta do.

13:12.731 --> 13:15.256
We have to get rid of the body,
clean up the mess...

13:15.434 --> 13:18.301
...then act like nothing's happened.
- Good plan. Except.

13:18.470 --> 13:20.267
- Except what?
- Say cheese.

13:20.773 --> 13:21.865
What are you doing?

13:22.041 --> 13:25.101
Making sure I get to drive your car
whenever I want to.

13:25.711 --> 13:29.112
- What? Give me that.
- Too late. I emailed it to myself.

13:29.281 --> 13:31.374
- You're bluffing.
- Perhaps.

13:31.550 --> 13:34.610
But can you really afford
to take that chance?

13:38.424 --> 13:42.087
&lt;i>Hush, little baby, don't say a word&lt;/i>

13:42.261 --> 13:45.788
&lt;i>Daddy's gonna buy you a mockingbird&lt;/i>

13:45.965 --> 13:48.433
&lt;i>If that mockingbird don't sing&lt;/i>

13:48.600 --> 13:51.160
Forget it, I'm not sleepy.

13:52.938 --> 13:54.462
Let's go in the hot tub.

13:55.474 --> 13:57.772
But I don't have a bathing suit.

13:58.377 --> 14:00.470
Me neither.

14:02.614 --> 14:04.878
Come on, stroke.

14:08.988 --> 14:11.456
Judith, ah. This just keeps getting better.

14:13.425 --> 14:16.861
Oh, hey, look who's up. Hi, sweetie.

14:17.029 --> 14:20.157
You need a change? Oh, yeah.

14:20.332 --> 14:22.960
I'll let you in on a little secret.

14:23.135 --> 14:24.466
Before this day is over...

14:24.636 --> 14:28.003
...I might need to change my undies too.

14:33.579 --> 14:34.841
Uh-oh.

14:35.014 --> 14:36.504
It's your Mommy again.

14:37.449 --> 14:38.643
Shh.

14:39.184 --> 14:40.310
Hello?

14:40.486 --> 14:42.477
Oh, hey, Judith. What's up?

14:42.654 --> 14:45.088
- So how's Laguna?
- Laguna's fine.

14:45.257 --> 14:47.225
Um, my mother's
not answering the phone.

14:47.426 --> 14:49.417
I need you to go check on her
and the baby.

14:49.595 --> 14:53.622
Me? You want me to drive all the way
to Sherman Oaks...

14:53.799 --> 14:57.428
...to check on your mother,
who you assured me was clean and sober?

15:00.172 --> 15:01.366
What's that?

15:01.540 --> 15:05.237
Uh, that is TV that I am watching.

15:05.844 --> 15:08.369
The baby channel.

15:08.547 --> 15:11.015
A documentary about obese babies.

15:11.183 --> 15:12.946
Tragic.

15:14.353 --> 15:18.847
I will check up on your mother for you,
but you owe me one.

15:19.024 --> 15:20.889
Oh, Alan.

15:21.060 --> 15:22.687
Ta-da.

15:27.032 --> 15:28.124
Not bad.

15:29.101 --> 15:30.432
What's not bad?

15:30.602 --> 15:34.732
I mean, it's not a bad idea
for me to check up on her.

15:34.907 --> 15:37.933
Thank you. Call me when you get there.

15:38.110 --> 15:40.544
Oh, Judith.

15:41.613 --> 15:44.047
Look who mowed the front lawn.

15:49.388 --> 15:52.448
So we're agreed,
we will never speak of this again.

15:52.624 --> 15:55.593
Well, that kind of depends on you,
doesn't it?

15:56.228 --> 16:00.130
I've already got the shovel, Jake.
I can dig another hole.

16:00.732 --> 16:02.495
Charlie, I'm home.

16:06.004 --> 16:07.938
Hey, sweetie, how was work?

16:08.107 --> 16:10.905
Okay. I was worried about Sir Lancelot.
Have you seen him?

16:11.076 --> 16:13.340
No, haven't seen him. Not a trace.

16:14.213 --> 16:15.237
What about you, Jake?

16:15.414 --> 16:17.780
No. But if I was a cat,
I'd be out on the beach.

16:17.950 --> 16:21.408
Because the beach is one big litter box
and the ocean is a giant fish bowl.

16:21.587 --> 16:23.521
Like having a sushi bar in your bathroom.

16:25.324 --> 16:27.758
Wow, how great would that be?

16:28.393 --> 16:31.453
I guess. I'll still feel better
when he comes back.

16:31.630 --> 16:33.393
We all will.

16:35.267 --> 16:39.670
- You're quite the little liar, aren't you?
- I'm 15. My life depends on it.

16:39.838 --> 16:41.897
Chelsea, Charlie's gonna take me driving.

16:42.074 --> 16:45.441
- Can we bring you back anything?
No, thanks.

16:52.050 --> 16:54.280
That woman just cut you off.

16:54.987 --> 16:58.320
Learn how to drive, you whore!

16:58.490 --> 17:00.822
Yeah, I'm talking to you!

17:00.993 --> 17:03.325
Lenore, we should probably keep it down.

17:03.495 --> 17:05.554
- We don't wanna wake the baby.
- What baby?

17:06.165 --> 17:08.156
Oh, right.

17:08.333 --> 17:10.233
Woof.

17:16.375 --> 17:18.809
Hello, Judith.

17:18.977 --> 17:21.912
I was about to call you.
The baby's fine, nothing to worry about.

17:22.080 --> 17:25.174
Hey, Judy, Judy, Judy!

17:25.617 --> 17:27.585
Yeah, yeah. That's her.

17:27.753 --> 17:30.051
Uh-huh. Blotto.

17:30.222 --> 17:33.385
Uh, no. No need to rush home.
Everything's under control.

17:33.592 --> 17:36.186
We're in the car,
Millie's sleeping in the back seat...

17:36.361 --> 17:38.056
...and we're heading for Malibu.

17:39.364 --> 17:41.264
Ehab-ray.

17:41.833 --> 17:43.892
Ehab-ray?

17:44.636 --> 17:49.096
You said you were taking me
for crab cakes at Gladstone's.

17:49.274 --> 17:52.641
Well, I'm sorry,
but you just don't have a choice here.

17:52.811 --> 17:56.713
- The hell I don't.
- Lenore! Lenore! Lenore!

17:56.882 --> 17:59.510
Red light. Slow down, slow down, stop!

18:02.254 --> 18:05.246
You're making me really nervous,
you know that?

18:13.632 --> 18:16.465
Hey, you mind
getting me another grape soda?

18:16.635 --> 18:20.435
- Yeah, I mind. Get it yourself.
- Fine.

18:20.606 --> 18:24.098
I just have to send this JPEG
to Chelsea real fast.

18:25.477 --> 18:27.502
Okay, okay.

18:28.146 --> 18:30.774
- Look who finally came home.
- Who?

18:31.717 --> 18:35.676
Sir Lancelot. You've been a bad kitty cat.

18:35.854 --> 18:39.051
I've been so worried about you.

18:41.927 --> 18:43.758
Okay, I'm confused.

18:43.929 --> 18:47.160
If that's Sir Lancelot,
then what did we squash?

18:47.332 --> 18:50.597
Your hope of ever getting behind
the wheel of my car again.

18:52.271 --> 18:53.602
Oh, man.

18:56.375 --> 18:59.344
Leverage is a fickle bitch, my friend.

19:01.980 --> 19:03.777
I got it.

19:07.986 --> 19:09.783
- Can I help you?
- Sorry to bother you.

19:09.955 --> 19:12.651
I live down the beach
and I'm looking for my cat.

19:13.458 --> 19:17.451
I'm sorry, I haven't seen it.
In fact, I just found my little guy.

19:18.330 --> 19:20.264
I'm really worried.

19:21.333 --> 19:23.460
He's black and white, about yay big.

19:23.635 --> 19:24.966
Answers to Puss-Puss.

19:25.637 --> 19:27.332
I'll keep an eye out for him.

19:27.506 --> 19:30.270
Looks like the fickle bitch is back.
